  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or build it with `vite build` here, so none of the rendering has been seen.\n\n- **Floor and backdrop:** a custom-geometry cove, with a flat light-grey floor that curves up through a quarter circle into a vertical wall.\n- **Spheres:** three spheres of the same diameter (1.5) in a row.\n  - Left is clear glass (transmission, a slight tint, IOR 1.5, strong environment reflection).\n  - Centre is brushed steel (fully metallic, anisotropic, procedural brushed texture).\n  - Right is dark red fabric (roughness 1, no metal, strong sheen, fine procedural weave normal).\n- **Lighting:**\n  - A studio environment gives the metal and glass something to reflect.\n  - A big soft key light casts the shadows, with a softbox travelling alongside it for broad reflections.\n  - A dimmer cool fill comes from the opposite side, and a rim light from behind.\n  - Contact shadows and anti-aliasing are added.\n- **Camera:** fixed, raised and three-quarter front, with all three spheres centred.\n- **Animation and state:** the key light and softbox drift side to side on a sine curve every frame. `window.__TASK_STATE__` holds the three sphere names and the current `keyLightX`, updated each frame. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set once the first frame has drawn.\n\nI avoided top-level await so the default Vite target builds. The glass opacity, shadow softness and light intensities are untuned guesses, so those are the first things to adjust once you see a frame.",
